description:
Trigger: client sends { "filter": <non-deserializable shape> } to /query or /queryChanges. validate_metadata_filter at metadata.rs:560-563 does:

  match serde_json::from_value(filter_val.clone()) {
      Ok(f) => f,
      Err(_) => return Ok(()),  // silent pass-through
  };

Per the rustdoc at line 549-552, this is intentional: 'fails to deserialize at all (the generic will surface the deserialize failure as unsupportedFilter, which is the spec-correct error for malformed filter shape)'.

This is correct in the happy case where generic handle_query's optional_arg with JmapError::unsupported_filter (jmap-server/handlers.rs:251-252) does in fact re-parse and report unsupportedFilter. Verified by reading that code: it does.

So this is NOT a correctness bug. The double-parse is a minor efficiency concern (filed at P2 below if interesting). Closing this as non-finding.
